text My father is sprawled out in the living room, like he always is.
text @[Tomoya]
text Hey.
text I touch his shoulders as they move up and down with his breathing.
text I would've been fine with a phone call or a letter, but Nagisa said it had to be this way.
text ─You have to meet him and tell him in person that you won't be back for a while.
text She said that because of the foolish thought that telling him might be enough to solve everything.
text It'll change nothing, though.
text I know this all too well. I know him, all too well.
sound K7Q.aac
text @[Father]
text Mm...?
text He could just be talking in his sleep, but my father groans.
text @[Tomoya]
text I'm leaving the house...
text I decide for myself that he's awake and start talking.
text @[Tomoya]
text And I'm not planning on coming back for a while, so...
text @[Tomoya]
text Good luck on your own, okay...?
text That's all I tell him before leaving his side.
